Z||000012||Fformula88||10-04-2001||02:51 PM||||I don't see why you wouldn't wax them once in a while  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif">  Mine are black, but they are all painted/coated with a finish that needs to be cared for like the paint on the car.  Ever try to clean wheels that have not had the brake dust removed in a while?  The finish gets stained and its very hard to get clean!  It keeps them protected... and being black it makes them very shiney  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000013||Tigger||10-04-2001||02:59 PM||||Has anyone tried no-stick Pam?<P>Hehe, just don't spray it on with the wheel on the car.||||reg||3
Z||000014||Rick 88||10-04-2001||03:24 PM||||I would spend at least ten minutes per cleaning my black lace wheels. Now they are very clean and in my storeroom. My 17's are much easier to clean. Yeah, regularly I even pull them off to clean the backside as well.<BR>I even clean the inner fenders at the same time.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Rick 88||||reg||1
